{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1216950-what-is-the-end-game-for-a-solar-circle","id":1216950,"title":"What is the end game for a Solar Circle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-09T04:57:15-07:00","id":1216950,"title":"What is the end game for a Solar Circle?","content":"So, I was thinking about this the other day, and I couldn't for the life of me figure it out...<br /> <br /> When playing a DB Exalt, the purpose is - generally speaking - take the throne and rule. That seems pretty clear to me. I know there are other aims/goals, but it seems like ruling the throne is kind of the assumed end game. So, what is that end game for Solars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:05:33-07:00","id":1216952,"title":"","content":"Would &quot;most&quot; DBs even <i>want</i> the throne? If one thing is clear in the Realm, is that no one wants another scarlet empress.<br /> <br /> What about a forest witch? Theirs is a dream of a wonderful, eternal afterlife.<br /> <br /> And that's just looking at a couple factions.<br /> That's nothing on the story of a captivating cathak in a quest to rediscover what honor means to him.<br /> The lost egg that died stopping a devil from destroying his home died a very satisfactory death.<br /> <br /> What of the lookshy taimyo that reforms the seventh legion and reinstates the shogunate across much of the threshold, and then gets to watch first hand its overtaking of the Realm... and retires to rest on those laurels?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure &quot;what is the end game for xxxxxxxxx&quot; is even a valid question if xxxxxxxxx isn't particularly specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:07:33-07:00","id":1216954,"title":"","content":"What <i>isn't</i> the end game for Solars? Heck, what isn't the end game for DBs? I feel like it's dictated mainly by individual character motivations. Maybe this character wants to be a king. Maybe this character just wants to avenge her mom. Maybe this character wants to find new expanses of lore and knowledge. <br /> <br /> Dragonblooded of the Scarlet Empire don't all necessarily want to be the next Empress---even those who would like to be the Empress may not actually be shooting for that goal. You'll probably get a lot who want to rise high in their House, be honored and successful, kick some Anathema butt. They're honestly not inherently less varied than Solars in terms of endgame, it's just that the lore and setting put a lot more structure around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:36:34-07:00","id":1216955,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'll clarify. It seems to me that the built-in kind of end-game goal for DB's is taking the throne. I know that can vary wildly from game to game. But I fee like that goal is very clearly built in as &quot;The End Game.&quot; But there doesn't seem to be anything even remotely like that built in.<br /> <br /> Once again, not saying eveyr DB game - or even every DB - has/should have the goal of taking the throne. But it does seem like that's kind of how their lore is set up. And there isn't an equivalent in the Solar book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:47:11-07:00","id":1216959,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't think that's accurate, even just for Dynasts---I don't really think there's a specific built-in endgame. It might be more true to say that the lore offers a sort of basic, general Dynastic progression of increasing their power, legacy, and influence within their House and the Realm in general. However, that soft endgame, if it exists, isn't as specific as taking the Scarlet Throne.<br /> <br /> Unless you just meant &quot;taking the throne&quot; in a much more general sense of becoming more powerful and influential, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:49:01-07:00","id":1216961,"title":"","content":"I still have to ask: Why?<br /> The Realm civil war is definitely a looming, large threat, with lots of outlying factors to complicate it, but why &quot;get the throne&quot; seems built-in for you?<br /> <br /> The &quot;built-in&quot; endgame I see is &quot;win/stop the civil war&quot; and its analogues, but I'm not sure how much of an endgame it actually is either. It's just a looming threat that makes you worry about every other looming threat at the same time. It's the tipping point, the verge of a small apocalypse. And that's just the main db faction, there's about as many dbs in other groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> And this world? It's the same world for solars. The Realm, big as it is, is a major consideration for everyone that isn't past the very edges of far-off civilization, if at least in the sense that &quot;if they explode we are in the blast radius&quot;.<br /> The Realm, as one of the biggest forces in the game bent on destroying solars whenever they can, are a common antagonist for solars and lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not, I feel, that DBs have a set endgame, but that they built the world around them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:50:09-07:00","id":1216962,"title":"","content":"I mean...<br /> <br /> The &quot;default&quot; Solar game is...also about taking the throne. Conquering Creation and forging a new Grand Solar Empire is pretty baseline as Solar games go, often with a side of &quot;we're not power hungry tyrants, really, we're just doing this to get everybody to work together to fight (Insert Big Scary World Ending Doom).&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:52:21-07:00","id":1216963,"title":"","content":"&quot;Take the throne and rule&quot; is as valid an end game for solars as it is for dragon blooded. <br /> <br /> Might be a different throne, might not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:57:15-07:00","id":1216964,"title":"","content":"So while I think 3rd ed was gone away form the one end for all metaplot (And hurrah for that) i will try to put down some possible ends to a solar game, which focuses nation/creationwide change.<br /> The ones i have seen alooted (with a few twitches of my own) to a bit abbriged. <br /> <br /> Reclamation - Solars save the world all avenger style<br /> <br /> Take Back what was lost - Topple the Realm and bring back the deliberative from the first age<br /> <br /> Into a new age - Bring Creation into a new age of technology, new political system and new themes (like steampunk, modern or all the way to future sci-fi)<br /> <br /> Kill that which can't be killed... again - Defeat the deathlords and forever kill the Neverborn<br /> <br /> The locust countercrusade - The seal to auto.world opens and the locust crusade starts. The solars defeat the crusade and drive their own crusade into auto. Ends up curing Autobot himself.<br /> <br /> Defeat the dragon - Kukla awakens and is defeated by solars. This fight uses Creation's landscape as kaijus uses Tokyo/other big city.<br /> <br /> Bend the wyld - The solars take the area around the pole back. Marching further into deeper wyld and making new lands. In the end Creation becomes round and the setting becomes a setting we now more from our real world aka space is made.<br /> <br /> Regain the Grace of our Father - enter the jade dome in heaven and redeem the solars in the eyes of UCS. That and get the other incarnates away from the celestial x-box.<br /> <br /> These are just examples. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bouns: On a personal level the fight against the great curse could be campaign goal in it self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:10:52-07:00","id":1216966,"title":"","content":"I'm sure one common goal for Solar circles is to replace the Empire with something better and rule Creation benevolently, but as others have said, the number of goals for a Solar circle is pretty much infinite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:13:29-07:00","id":1216967,"title":"","content":"And that's just a set of endgames for &quot;builders&quot;. Some people just want to sail into the sunset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:30:08-07:00","id":1216974,"title":"","content":"I think the setting and lore tend to perhaps push forward certain types of endgames to each splat. The whole &quot;returning rulers&quot; Solars angle makes &quot;take the throne&quot; endgames easy to go for, and &quot;defeat BIG SCARY THING&quot; is pretty heavily reinforced too... but honestly you can do almost anything if the players and ST put their minds to it. If you want to make a Solar Circle who serve a Deathlord because they think that's the best path for their righteous excellence, you totally can (there's even a canon Solar in 2e who does just that).<br /> <br /> With DBs, there's a a general push for &quot;protect and empower the societal framework that places you on a pedestal, and increase your influence therein&quot;. However, it's just as valid to have DBs strike out on their own to forge their own kingdom. In fact, in some ways, it could be even easier; DBs are allowed to be openly Exalted and don't have to worry about people rejecting them out of hand for being Anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T07:15:30-07:00","id":1216988,"title":"","content":"I was going to chime in... but I think everyone else has covered it. Defeat a big bad or rule a prosperous kingdom* seem like the main goals, but if your PCs' motivation is to become the greatest artist in Creation, then it's likely a rather different endgame.<br /> <br /> *One key difference I think with 3rd ed, is the focus a little lower, so it's more plausible to rule <i><u>a</u></i>kingdom as your end goal, rather than rule <i><u>every</u></i>kingdom.<br /> <br /> To give an example, in the fairly long-running 2nd ed game I ran, the game ended with the PCs stopping Walker in Darkness from destroying the world with the Sword of Creation, and being involved in putting the Neverborn to a deeper sleep so that they were no longer ordering the Deathlords to destroy Creation. They also used a sub-system of the Sword (the World-Denying Solipsism Protocol) to mostly (though not entirely) close off Malfeas from Creation, making the Reclamation much harder.<br /> <br /> In my 3rd ed game (set 25 years later, with most but not all of the same characters), the game ended with the sorcerer-queen ruling a magical mountain kingdom, the Djala warlord controlling the four Djala kingdoms, the Full Moon being decadent king of a desert city, and the Zenith having spread the Cult of the Illuminated and called a conclave of southern Solars to organise the Cult (as Kether Rock had been destroyed and the Cult shattered during those 25 years). Also, most of the neighbouring kingdoms were either their puppets, or too weak to strike at them due to PCs murdering/cursing their rulers.<br /> <br /> So that's an example of the two main end-games: defeating the Big Bad and saving the world, and ruling your own kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Of course, the problem is that these aren't really end-goals that... end. Going into retirement ends the story. Becoming king of a country? Well, you've then got to actually rule. Defeating a Big Bad? Well, there's plenty of other Big Bads out there.<br /> It's a reasonable place to stop the game of course (which is what I did).<br /> <br /> But it's not really the end. So now my friend is running a 3rd game with most of the same PCs (not all) as my game, in the same setting. So now we see the sorceress's magical kingdom threatened by Realm invasion, the Djala kingdom facing a severe overpopulation crisis (because the Twilight had given all the Djala doubled lifespans and Exalted Healing), the Cult of the Illuminated being oppressed by the countries whose rulers the PCs murdered, and someone unleashing insane moonsilver eidolons with the memories of the Lunar PC's first-age incarnation.<br /> So the circle's end-game here is really back to defeating the Big Bad, this time the Realm rather than Walker in Darkness, as well as a number of... Little Bads?<br /> <br /> I feel this is possibly relevant: <a href=\"https://www.smbc-comics.com/comics/1525725208-soonish39.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.smbc-comics.com/comics/1...-soonish39.png</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-09-2018, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T07:16:21-07:00","id":1216989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1216950-what-is-the-end-game-for-a-solar-circle?p=1216967#post1216967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's just a set of endgames for &quot;builders&quot;. Some people just want to sail into the sunset.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a boat so big the it flips flat earth Creation like a disc as it nears the edge of the world. :-P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T07:46:26-07:00","id":1216993,"title":"","content":"The end game for my Dawn caste Solar was to kick the frakkin\u2019 Realm out of his town so that he could tend his bar in peace. Of course, the world will never let him do that, so he strives to smooth out the bumps around him, but always at his heart he just wants some peace.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s kind of everybody\u2019s story to some degree. Look at Hawkeye in the Marvel movies. Immanent threats interrupt your plans and have to be dealt with - and some of them go on to have world-shaking consequences which your character may be a big part of - but that doesn\u2019t mean every solar has to want to rule the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T08:25:20-07:00","id":1217001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1216950-what-is-the-end-game-for-a-solar-circle?p=1216964#post1216964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Bend the wyld - The solars take the area around the pole back. Marching further into deeper wyld and making new lands. In the end Creation becomes round and the setting becomes a setting we now more from our real world aka space is made.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is our current &quot;endgame&quot;, our 3 year running campaign, has been about getting to a point where we can Wyld Shape a huge new land on the southwest. We've deliberately kept away from the Realm/Threshold to avoid attention and been forging our empire in the outskirts of Creation.<br /> <br /> I think in around 3-4 sessions we'll launch our Wyld Expedition and start the Shaping, which we antecipate will take many sessions. I've approached our ST with an offer to be assistant ST for this, and am trying to get us to build some beefed up DBs to play the Wyld Shape Encounters as, switching to our Solars only when Behemoths appear ( and with the amount of rolls we are planning to get, there will be quite a few ), and otherwise using our Solars as &quot;buff beacons&quot; and &quot;safe zones&quot; during the battles.<br /> <br /> We're playing this as our Solar Circle being the Gods of this New Land, beings that trasversed the Chaos and Created this World, somewhat like Egyptian Gods (or a few other pantheons, too). Once we get this done, we will play conquering this land. We will switch between worldbuilding with our Solars, with our regular ST, and a more low level varied &quot;mission&quot; stories, with new DB characters who are part of our Solars' retinue, assigned to them by the Expedition Force, STed by me.<br /> <br /> These missions will be varied, such as diplomatic overture to natives, war with natives, monster hunting, mapping of places of power, collection of precious resources, establishment of outposts Wyld Border inspection, etc...<br /> <br /> So yeah... no real &quot;end&quot; to the endgame in sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-09-2018, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:22:43-07:00","id":1217018,"title":"","content":"Weather the Time of Tumult and prepare to enter the Third Age of Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:28:11-07:00","id":1217020,"title":"","content":"Claiming the Realm is your own just means you have to wage a global war against the Lunar Exalted and the Deathlords while competing against the Guild for wealth and influence and fending off the machinations of the Sidereal Exalted and their grand design. <br /> <br /> The game doesn't end until the players have accomplished everything they set out to do, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:29:51-07:00","id":1217021,"title":"","content":"I'd say the &quot;endgame&quot; is to no longer be hunted.<br /> Either because you've murdered your way to the top, teamed up with old enemies to save the world or because you've gotten so strong that they simply don't think it's worth attacking you unless you're attacking them.<br /> <br /> They're all good places for the curtain to drop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:31:51-07:00","id":1217024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1216950-what-is-the-end-game-for-a-solar-circle?p=1217021#post1217021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the &quot;endgame&quot; is to no longer be hunted.<br /> Either because you've murdered your way to the top, teamed up with old enemies to save the world or because you've gotten so strong that they simply don't think it's worth attacking you unless you're attacking them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's interesting; to survive through to a shift in the world order such that Solars can take a place on the stage without being so thoroughly outfunded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T11:52:13-07:00","id":1217071,"title":"","content":"I've always had Solar endgame be downtime measured in centuries, and high risk of becoming a shining example of why the usurpation happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T18:05:41-07:00","id":1217212,"title":"","content":"To go back to the social roles theory that I've put forth before:<br /> <br /> The &quot;default&quot; Dragon-Blooded endgame is to become the ruler of the Realm because the Dragon-Blooded are the social Establishment, and being the top member of the power structure is the ultimate expression of achievement/progress as a member of the establishment. There are other possible Dragon-Blooded stories, but this is the fairly obvious greatest ambition.<br /> <br /> The &quot;default&quot; Sidereal endgame is to become the leader of the foremost Sidereal faction and puppeteer of Heaven, because the Sidereals are the Secret Masters, and being the master conspirator is the ultimate expression of achievement/progress as a conspirator. There are other possible Sidereal stories, but this is the fairly obvious greatest ambition.<br /> <br /> The &quot;default&quot; Solar endgame is to transform Creation, because Solars are the Great Men* who impose a vision on the world, bending the course of nations. The <i>specific</i> transformation is necessarily unique to each Solar, because the whole Great Man* concept is that they break the world's old paradigms and do something new. If the Solar is an Exalted Napoleon, it'll look something like the Dragon-Blooded endgame, except that she comes from outside of the establishment instead of from inside it. But other kinds of Solars will do other things; you could have a religious messiah, an abolitionist whose social movement turns all Creation against slavery, the sorcerer who brings Creation into contact with Autochthonia, the explorer who sailed west into the Wyld until she opened the way to continent thought lost because of the Baloran Crusade, etc.<br /> <br /> *The gender-loading here is simply because the historiographical theory/model being adapted for fiction/gaming here is known as the &quot;Great Man&quot; approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T18:37:13-07:00","id":1217224,"title":"","content":"I'd amend all the &quot;become Realm Ruler&quot; with &quot;become local ruler&quot;. Lookshy and Parsad matter, people! Throw off the chains of the realm, become ruler of Parsad! Establish your own dynasty!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T19:11:19-07:00","id":1217235,"title":"","content":"Mind, between my personal world view and my perspective on the Great Curse, I envision the ideal end game for any given Solar to consist of finding a way to reconcile their own personality flaws with the complexity of the world in a manner other than trying to have absolute mastery over everything, accepting the limitations of power and control and engaging with people and the world more on their own terms, and dedicating power more to purposes of understanding, personal and societal benefits and improvement, and creating the stage in which people can find self-actualisation and enlightenment, while continuously navigating the difficulties that emerge from many complex parts grating against one another, and protecting against those threats that come from the Outside.<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause they tried the whole &quot;take over the world&quot; thing before, and it didn't really work out for them. For all that one might refer to Great Man Theory, it's interesting that the Solars fell beneath the weight of a dissatisfied majority. Not to mention any portrayal of the First Age (which is kind of most of them) that presents it as having continuously generated challenges and rebellions for them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't really see the solution to that being &quot;do it all over again, but Even Harder&quot;. Oh sure, it makes for a compelling and resonant narrative when people just repeat the mistakes of the past and set themselves back on a trajectory of disaster in the next few millennia, but I'm willing to indulge myself with a bit of my own idealised setting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Embrace Powerlessness.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T19:44:10-07:00","id":1217245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1216950-what-is-the-end-game-for-a-solar-circle#post1216950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was thinking about this the other day, and I couldn't for the life of me figure it out...<br /> <br /> When playing a DB Exalt, the purpose is - generally speaking - take the throne and rule. That seems pretty clear to me. I know there are other aims/goals, but it seems like ruling the throne is kind of the assumed end game. So, what is that end game for Solars?</div> </div> </div> </div>End game is for your characters to complete their Motivations and do epic things along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T19:59:54-07:00","id":1217249,"title":"","content":"... Sidereal endgame is to either kill thebad guys and save the world and then make out with a cute ex-enemy on the beach...or die saving the world and nobody ever finds out about your sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Sidereal are spy movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T20:26:24-07:00","id":1217255,"title":"","content":"Oh, just had an idea for DB PC campaign I might ST...<br /> <br /> What if as a reward for completing certain missions the Solar Sages (our Solar pcs) offered enlightened training (actual Experience points through Flowing Mind Prana branch of Lore)? But also grant certain Intimacies with them?<br /> <br /> They offer gifts of sorcerous initiations (through Summonings and Crafting), gifts of spells and blessings.<br /> <br /> Will you ride the Tide of Enlightenment, swim against it, or be washed away by it?<br /> <br /> As Solars PCs it will be a good opportunity to explore the Burden of Divinity. Be exposed to limit triggers and interact with that. But only to a player agreed extent.<br /> <br /> What Intimacies will they instill on their DB PCs, what powers do they hand them? What do they expect in return?<br /> <br /> All this in a exceptionally Wyld Shaped continent. A geomantic marvel of myriad legendary places of power to be harvested and improved. Hearthstones, manse building... Too bad Towers of the Mighty is still so far away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:39:20-07:00","id":1217345,"title":"","content":"I want a combined Sidereal and Solar endgame of overthrowing the Celestials in Yu Shan and taking over the Games of Divinity and leaving Creation to the normal humans. Keep the cycle going and make everything worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T20:49:02-07:00","id":1217574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1216950-what-is-the-end-game-for-a-solar-circle?p=1217021#post1217021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the &amp;quot;endgame&amp;quot; is to no longer be hunted.<br /> Either because you've murdered your way to the top, teamed up with old enemies to save the world or because you've gotten so strong that they simply don't think it's worth attacking you unless you're attacking them.<br /> <br /> They're all good places for the curtain to drop.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the older Civilization games you could win by building the &quot;World Bank&quot; wonder, at which point you became so necesary to the global economy that fighting you is effectively impossible. From Discworld, the Patrician of Ankh-Morpork is safe because as much as everyone hates him, every other option is worse and everyone knows it. In 2e, my character succceeded in destroying his (lesser) Great House and became to vital to Guild, Realm Economy, and the Scavenger lands that even the Mask of Winters wouldn't openly move against him. <br /> <br /> Until we accidentally destroyed the world on behalf of the Neverborn, we had a good thing going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T05:24:17-07:00","id":1217631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1216950-what-is-the-end-game-for-a-solar-circle?p=1217245#post1217245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> End game is for your characters to complete their Motivations and do epic things along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the closest thing to my perspective I've seen so far. But I would go further (maybe too far?) and say that:<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't designed to have an &quot;endgame&quot; in the first place, because it's not a game with an end state. Being an RPG means it &quot;ends&quot; when folks decide they want to start again (even then new characters might start in the world the previous ones created) or play something else, or just stop showing up. Even a big goal like &quot;take the throne&quot; isn't naturally an end state, because now you have a throne. What are you going to DO with it? Who is going to try to take it from you next? Does anyone really get the impression that ruling in Creation is less fraught then conquering? <br /> <br /> Instead, I would think of stories having &quot;closure&quot; instead of a game having an &quot;end&quot;. And closure is going to be based, as AnubisXy indicates, on the specific motivations of the characters, but also the players. If taking the throne happens to wrap things up neatly for everyone and creates a natural stopping point, then great. But I don't think there's anything particularly &quot;default&quot; about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T05:30:26-07:00","id":1217633,"title":"","content":"Said another way, I have a hard time imagining the circle of Dragon-blooded whose shared ambition is taking the throne being the creation of a group of players who would want to stop playing once they got it.<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe? But to me that seems pretty atypical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 05-11-2018, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T03:49:00-07:00","id":1217925,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I don't quite agree, I can see a fair few players for whom the fun is cutting/intriguing your way to the throne; not the bureaucratic and stressful task of actually running things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T05:35:25-07:00","id":1217934,"title":"","content":"Why even assume that the person wearing the crown and sitting the throne is going to run things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T06:01:37-07:00","id":1217941,"title":"","content":"Oh, indeed!<br /> <br /> Actually, in the DB games my friend's play, once a PC got to the throne she immediately went into seclusion to avoid assassination.<br /> <br /> Thus, in a later campaign, the PCs were fighting other big players about who gets access to the Empress, and who gets to run things on a day-to-day basis.<br /> <br /> Thus, at the end of the campaign, one PC was grand admiral, another Prime Minister, another supreme general, another head of the All-Seeing Eye, etc.<br /> <br /> But, at that point again, the game ended. The ST started again with a new, 0xp game, with those old PCs in the background.<br /> <br /> Because seizing power and ruling are quite different games, and if seizing power is something that takes years of real-life gaming, then you may well want to say &quot;We've won, let's play a new game.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of the people I play with are very much in favour of continual games and stories, where there's no endgame, but I've found I prefer a big, dramatic, planned end, rather than a game just stretching out indefinitely until it burns out.<br /> I ran 2nd ed for a few years, but it started getting worse as I ran out of ideas. So I picked a distinct end; Walker in Darkness, whose forces the PCs had often clashed with, was going to destroy the world, and they had to stop him. Somewhat classic.<br /> <br /> When I ran 3rd ed, I found it more and more difficult (and stressful) to run over time, as it was quite awkward to run a game with 6 essence 5 characters with nothing more than the Core Book. So, working from what PCs were doing, I set up for another end. The god ascended to Heaven, the warlord took over the jungle, the sorceress-queen united the tribes and created her magical kingdom, and the circle of enemy Solar NPCs were finally run to ground and defeated.<br /> <br /> Some players were quite happy with that. Others wanted to go with what's next: Now they rule their kingdoms, what issues do they face? What challenges? <br /> <br /> Because of this, one of the players has taken over the game, and is now running what happens next (the Realm's invading, the jungle kingdom's imploding, two of the PCs are going to war). I'm enjoying the game a lot actually... but I kind of wonder if I'd have enjoyed a brand new game more. The other players have mixed feelings (one's dropped out, others are enthusiastic, others don't mind either way).<br /> <br /> I play another game which I like, which we've been playing for maybe 8 years? Sometimes it's okay but not great (mostly when the ST tries to let the PCs go sandbox... they're very unmotivated PCs, so it doesn't work well, but that's not the STs fault), sometimes it's really good (when the ST does longer plots with distinct goals and antagonists, like the current Nephwrack plot, or when we were trying to make peace between two warring emperors). But again, I kind of wonder if it would be better to have ended it with a suitable plotline, and started a new game.<br /> <br /> The thing of course, is that not everyone has the same ideas of what they want as an end-point, and that's certainly what I've found. Some people want to play the same characters and story for a decade, others want to change characters every year but are fine with the story, others want to have short but memorable stories with distinct ends. Some people want to play &quot;found an empire&quot; but others want to play &quot;rule an empire&quot;, which are very different games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-12-2018, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}